1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,643
Two vials, five milligrams each.

2
00:00:02,643 --> 00:00:04,947
One gets two milliliters of water.

3
00:00:04,947 --> 00:00:06,302
The other gets five.

4
00:00:06,302 --> 00:00:08,177
Which vial holds more peptide?

5
00:00:08,177 --> 00:00:09,010
Neither.

6
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:10,768
Water never adds peptide.

7
00:00:10,768 --> 00:00:16,171
At two milliliters, the concentration is two point five milligrams per milliliter.

8
00:00:16,171 --> 00:00:19,882
At five milliliters, it is one milligram per milliliter.

9
00:00:19,882 --> 00:00:27,877
A portion of two hundred fifty micrograms takes zero point one milliliter from the first vial, and zero point two five from the second.

10
00:00:27,877 --> 00:00:29,166
Now divide it out.

11
00:00:29,166 --> 00:00:34,583
Five thousand micrograms, in portions of two hundred fifty, is twenty portions.

12
00:00:34,583 --> 00:00:35,468
Either way.

13
00:00:35,468 --> 00:00:39,947
More water means more volume per portion, never more portions.

14
00:00:39,947 --> 00:00:41,419
The math doesn't lie.

15
